{title: All Glory, Laud, and Honor}
{artist: Theodulf of Orléans · tr. John Mason Neale}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Chorus
[Bb]All glory, laud, and [F]honor to [Gm]thee, Re[F]deemer, [Bb]King,
to whom the lips of [F]children made [Gm]sweet ho[F]sannas [Bb]ring!

Verse 1
Thou [Bb]art the King of [F]Israel, thou [Gm]David's [F]royal [Bb]Son,
who in the Lord's name [F]comest, the [Gm]King and [F]blessed [Bb]one.

Verse 2
All glory, laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King,
To Whom the lips of children Made sweet hosannas ring.
The company of angels Are praising Thee on High,
And mortal men and all
things Created make reply.

Verse 3
All glory, laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King,
To Whom the lips of children Made sweet hosannas ring.
The people of the Hebrews With palms before Thee went;
Our prayer and praise and anthems Before Thee we present.

Verse 4
All glory, laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King,
To Whom the lips of children Made sweet hosannas ring.
To Thee, before Thy passion, They sang their hymns of praise;
To Thee, now high exalted, Our melody we raise.

Verse 5
All glory, laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King,
To Whom the lips of children Made sweet hosannas ring.
Thou didst accept their praises; Accept the prayers we bring,
Who in all good delightest, Thou good and gracious King.
